    ...
}
```

If `workersCount` is 1 (single worker), the loop `for i := 1; i < 1; i++` never executes, so no results are read at all! This would explain why the loaded cache appears empty - the single worker's result (which loads the data) is never waited for, and the function returns before the goroutine completes.

This is the bug. When there's only one data file (which happens with `SaveToFile` using concurrency=1), the load function doesn't wait for the goroutine to finish, returning an uninitialized/empty cache.

